### 2.13 Using `tagName()` method

HTML elements are defined by specific tag names such as `<input>`, `<div>`, `<p>`,` <a>`, and more. With the tag name locator strategy, we can locate elements by specifying their respective tag names.

Tag name locator strategy is less reliable for selecting single elements in Selenium as tag names alone are not always unique identifiers on a web page.

However, the tag name strategy can still be useful in certain scenarios, such as when selecting multiple elements of the same tag type

Choosing the appropriate locator strategy based on the uniqueness and stability of the element's attributes is crucial for reliable and maintainable test automation.

Here is the order of locator strategies in terms of significance, arranged in priority order.

