### Summary

- XML Path Language (XPath) is a language that allows us to navigate and search for specific elements within an HTML and XML document.
- Absolute XPath describes the exact location of an element within a document, starting from the root node.
- Using absolute XPath, the path to an element starts with `/html` and includes all parent elements until the desired element.
- The `By.xpath()` method in Selenium WebDriver allows locating elements using XPath expressions.
- The disadvantage of absolute XPath is that it becomes invalid if there are any changes in the path of the element.
- Relative XPath expressions are more flexible, as they depend on the element's relationship to other elements rather than the entire path from the root.

</Section>

