**Locating Username Input Element**

<Img imageSrc="https://new-assets.ccbp.in/frontend/content/qa-testing/images/qa-rm-8-username-inspect.png" alt="username input element">

From the HTML DOM tree the relative XPath is `//input[@id='username']`.

In the above XPath,

- The `//` signifies that the search can start from anywhere in the DOM structure.

- The `input` indicates that we are looking for an input element.

- `[@id='username']` specifies a condition to filter the input elements based on their `id` attribute. In this case, we are looking for an input element with the attribute `id` equal to `username`.

If we want to start from the `<div>` element that contains the password input field the relative XPath will be `//div//input[@id='username']`.

- `//div`: Selects any `<div>` element in the DOM tree, regardless of its position or level of nesting.
- `//input`: Selects any `<input>` element within the `<div>` element in the DOM tree, regardless of its position or level of nesting.
- `[@id='username']`: Selects the element with an `id` attribute equal to `username`.

**Adding Username Input Element**

