Here, 

<Img imageSrc="https://new-assets.ccbp.in/frontend/content/qa-testing/images/qa-rm-8-quotes-issue.png" widthPercent="80" alt="quotes issue">

Using double quotes around "username" causes a problem because the computer gets confused when it encounters the clash of double quotes.

The outer double quotes are used to define a string, but the inner double quotes are also used to enclose the value of the `id` attribute in the XPath expression.

This confusion makes it difficult for the computer to understand the intended meaning of the code.

<Img imageSrc="https://new-assets.ccbp.in/frontend/content/qa-testing/images/qa-rm-8-double-quotes-solved.png"widthPercent="80" alt="double quotes solver">

To resolve the issue, we need to either use single quotes inside the XPath expression or escape character the inner double quotes.

