### 2.2 Using `contains()` Function

The `contains()` can be used when we want to locate an element using partial text or partial attribute value.

#### Syntax

```text
//tagname[contains(@attribute, 'partial value')]
```

Here,

- `@attribute`: Attribute of the web element
- `partial value`: The Partial value of the attribute/text

We can also use the `text()` function in place of an attribute.

#### Example

```
//h1[contains(text(), 'Minifig')]
```

Here, we used partial text of the product title to locate the element.

