  </div>
  <div class="child">
    <p id="grandchild2">Grandchild 2</p>
  </div>
  <p class="child">Child 3</p>
</div>
```

For the above example, we can write the CSS selector expression as `div.parent>div:first-of-type`.

Here, the expression selects the first `<div>` child element inside the parent element`<div class="parent">` i.e., 

```
<div class="child">
  <p id="grandchild1">Grandchild 1</p>
</div>
```

