### 2.5 Last-of-type

The `last-of-type` selector allows us to select the last element of a specified type among a group of sibling elements. 

#### Syntax

```text
:last-of-type
```

#### Example

Let's write the expression to select the last `<div>` element (with "Grandchild 2" text).

```html
<div class="parent">
  <p class="child">Child 1</p>
  <p class="child">Child 2</p> 
  <div class="child">
    <p id="grandchild1">Grandchild 1</p>
  </div>
  <div class="child">
    <p id="grandchild2">Grandchild 2</p>
  </div>
  <p class="child">Child 3</p>
</div>
```

For the above example, we can write the CSS selector expression as `div.parent > div:last-of-type`.

Here, the expression selects the last `<div>` element inside the element`<div class="parent">` i.e., 

```
<div class="child">
  <p id="grandchild2">Grandchild 2</p>
</div>
```

