### 2.6 Nth-of-type

The `nth-of-type` selector allows us to select the Nth element of a specified type among a group of sibling elements. 


#### Syntax

```text
:nth-of-type(expression)
```

Here,

- `element` represents the current node.
- `:nth-of-type(expression)` selects the Nth child element based on the expression. 
- `expression` might be a _number_, or keyword like _even_, _odd_ etc. The _number_ will always **starts from 1**.

As we have learned earlier, we can create our own expression to select the Nth child element of a parent element as `3n`, `4n - 1` etc.

#### Example

Let's write the expression to select the second child element of the parent element `<div>`.

```html
<div class="parent">
  <p class="child">Child 1</p>
  <p class="child">Child 2</p> 
  <div class="child">
    <p id="grandchild1">Grandchild 1</p>
  </div>
  <div class="child">
    <p id="grandchild2">Grandchild 2</p>
  </div>
  <p class="child">Child 3</p>
</div>
```

For the above example, we can write the CSS selector expression as `div.parent > p:nth-of-type(2)`.

Here, the expression selects the second child element inside the `<div>` element containing the class name as `parent` i.e., `<p id="child2">Child 2</p>`.

