### Summary

- Pseudo-class Selectors
  - `first-child`: This selector allows us to select the first-child element among a group of sibling elements, regardless of its type.
  - `last-child`: This selector allows us to select the last-child element among a group of sibling elements, regardless of its type.
  - `nth-child`: This selector allows us to select elements based on their position among a group of sibling elements, regardless of its type.
  - `first-of-type`: This selector allows us to select the first element of a specified type among a group of sibling elements. 
  - `last-of-type`: This selector allows us to select the last element of a specified type among a group of sibling elements.
  - `nth-of-type`: This selector allows us to select the Nth element of a specified type among a group of sibling elements. 
- The flow of finding the elements is always a one way direction not a two way direction.
- CSS Selectors does not have the feature to locate elements based on the visible text.

