## 1. Writing Login Failure Case

In the previous unit, we wrote a test case for a successful login. Now, let's write a test case for a login failure. This test case will attempt to log in with invalid credentials and verify that the login attempt was unsuccessful.

We will use the same initial code as before, but this time, we will change the username and password to invalid values. We will also change the expected URL to the login page URL since the login attempt should fail and the user should remain on the login page.

To avoid repeating the above steps every time, we can utilize the initial code provided in the [Introduction](#introduction) section.

Here, in our test, we provide invalid credentials and verify that the login attempt was unsuccessful by checking the error message displayed on the web page when invalid credentials are provided.


```java
@Test
public void loginWithInvalidCredentials() {
     // Set the system property for Chrome driver with its path
        System.setProperty("webdriver.chrome.driver", "PATH_TO_CHROMEDRIVER");

        // Create a new instance of ChromeDriver
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        // Navigate to the login page
        driver.get("https://rahulnxttrendz.ccbp.tech/login");

        // Locate and enter valid username input field element by its id
        WebElement usernameEl = driver.findElement(By.id("username"));
        usernameEl.sendKeys("rahul");

        // Locate and enter invalid password input field element by its id
        WebElement passwordEl = driver.findElement(By.id("password"));
        passwordEl.sendKeys("rahul2021");

        // Find the login button element by its class name
        WebElement loginButtonEl = driver.findElement(By.className("login-button"));

        // Submit the login form
        loginButtonEl.submit();

        // Wait for the Error message to be loaded
        WebDriverWait wait = new WebDriverWait(driver, Duration.ofSeconds(10));
        wait.until(ExpectedConditions.visibilityOfElementLocated(By.className("error-message")));

        // Verify the error message
        WebElement errorMessageEl = driver.findElement(By.className("error-message"));
        String errorMessage = errorMessageEl.getText();
        Assert.assertEquals(errorMessage, "*username and password didn't match");

        // Close the browser
        driver.close();
}
```

