### 4. Initialize Web Elements Using PageFactory

#### Initializing Web Elements

In Selenium, the PageFactory class provides a method called **initElements()** for initializing all the web elements.

#### Syntax

```java
PageFactory.initElements(driver, this);
```
- `PageFactory` class provides a set of methods to initialize elements on a web page.
- The `initElements` method takes care of initializing our WebElements as defined by `@FindBy` or `@FindBys` annotations.
- `driver` is the WebDriver instance, which is used to locate elements.
- `this` refers to the current class object, which is used to define the context in which the fields should be initialized

#### Code

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.support.PageFactory;

public class LoginPageUsingPageFactory {
  WebDriver driver;
  ...
  public LoginPageUsingPageFactory(WebDriver driver) {
    this.driver = driver;
    PageFactory.initElements(driver, this);
  }
}

```

