```

In the above code, we can see that an exception has been thrown as we are trying to access the driver instance after we have closed all the browser instances.

</Section>

<Section>

### Summary


- Selenium WebDriver sees each window as a different entity.
- Identifying a window
    - `getWindowHandle()`: This method is used to obtain the unique identifier (or handle) of the current browser window that the driver has focused on.
    - `getWindowHandles()`: This method returns a set of window handles that can be used to iterate over all open windows of this WebDriver instance.
- The `driver.switchTo().window(ChildWindow);`  method is used switch among the windows.
- Closing Windows
  - `close()`: This method is used to close the current browser window or tab that has focus.
  - `quit()`: This method is used to terminate all the web browser sessions.

