https://rahulnxttrendz.ccbp.tech/login
https://www.facebook.com/
```

### 1.3 Refreshing the Page

In a web browser, we've likely clicked the "refresh" or "reload" button (or pressed `F5` or `Cmd + R` on keyboard) to reload the current web page. This action fetches the most recent content of the page from the server. Selenium WebDriver provides a method to simulate this action.

`driver.navigate().refresh()` method replicates the action of refreshing or reloading the current web page. It will re-fetch the page's content from the server, which can be particularly useful if we want to ensure that we're interacting with the most recent version of the web page during testing.

#### Code

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;

public class SeleniumExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Set the path to the chromedriver executable
        // Note: Replace '/path/to/chromedriver' with the actual path on Web system
        System.setProperty("webdriver.chrome.driver", "/path/to/chromedriver");

        // Create a new instance of ChromeDriver
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        // Navigate to another URL using the navigate().to() method
        driver.navigate().to("https://rahulnxttrendz.ccbp.tech/login");

        // Refresh the current page (this will reload "https://rahulnxttrendz.ccbp.tech/login")
        driver.navigate().refresh();

        // Close the browser after tasks are completed
        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

