### 3.10 Set Size of Browser Window

- `setSize(Dimension targetSize)` method sets the size of the browser window to a specified width and height.

- Setting specific browser sizes can help test responsive designs or how the application behaves in those dimensions.

#### Code:

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.Dimension;

public class SeleniumExample {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        // Set the path to the chromedriver executable
        // Note: Replace '/path/to/chromedriver' with the actual path on Web system
        System.setProperty("webdriver.chrome.driver", "/path/to/chromedriver");

        // Create a new instance of ChromeDriver
        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();
        Dimension newDimension = new Dimension(1024, 768);
        driver.manage().window().setSize(newDimension);

        // Close the browser after tasks are completed
        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

- In the context of `setSize`, the values `1024` and `768` represent the `width` and `height`, respectively, of the browser window in `pixels`.

